9v1 Corollary S3.1; the growing-depth consequence is the authored elementary deduction log log T_p=4p log p+O(p+log p) with epsilon_p=exp(-p^2). For SK, c_2=1/sqrt(2) matches the unordered-pair expectation after an independent mean-zero scalar diagonal offset. This does not show that the earlier near-optimal constructed words share a uniform angle bound, supply angle-selection complexity, or establish a growing-depth measurement tail. It is standalone context, not a prerequisite of the earlier SK QAOA construction or a selected formal endpoint.","citation_ids":["qaoa_finite_size_corollary","authored_bounded_angle_depth_comparison"],"evidence_ids":["ordinary_comparison_warrants_20261024"],"id":"circuit.later_finite_size_comparison","kind":"claim","label":"A later finite-size estimate for a bounded-angle class","locator":"Corollary S3.1, printed pp.46–47, equations (S3.1)–(S3.4), with cost-angle convention (S3.7). Statement inspected; full cavity proof not independently checked. Authored consequence: long §11.5.","source_id":"qaoa_finite_size_2026","statement":"For the source ordered-tuple Gaussian finite-degree mixture xi(t)=sum_q c_q^2 t^q, a depth p>=1 word with every cost angle bounded in absolute value by Gamma>0, and x>0 with xi(2),xi′(1),xi′′(33)<=x and Gamma^2 p^2 x>=1, set B_p=256p^4(2e Gamma^2 p^2 x)^p, E_p=70 Gamma^2 p^2 x+p log(2), R_p=(2E_p/log(2))^(2p). For 0<epsilon<=4 Gamma p x min(exp(-1/2),2^(-(8p^2+3)/100)), the disorder-averaged energy error |nu_n-nu_infinity| is at most epsilon whenever n>=T_p=max{2^(8p^2+3) B_p (2^(deg(xi)+4) Gamma^2 p^2 x^2/epsilon^2)^R_p [2 log_2(4 Gamma p x/epsilon)+deg(xi)]^2,16 Gamma p x/epsilon}. No mixer-angle bound is imposed. Consequently, for fixed mixture,Gamma,x, deterministic words with p(n)→infinity, one common cost-angle bound Gamma, and p(n)log p(n)=o(log log n) satisfy |nu_n(W_n)-nu_infinity(W_n)|<=exp(-p(n)^2) eventually.","status":"unverified"},"ref":"sha256:f22708f3180068944c06829213f78f6ecfb65ef34f6c8decded774b95a041d92/nodes/circuit.later_finite_size_comparison","relations":[{"derived":true,"family":"provenance","from":"sha256:f22708f3180068944c06829213f78f6ecfb65ef34f6c8decded774b95a041d92/nodes/circuit.later_finite_size_comparison","id":"field:4078847f97989e7fc34abd37c23452d47698a4f746e67baf5507c8ff0d29580c","kind":"source_id","owner_ref":"sha256:f22708f3180068944c06829213f78f6ecfb65ef34f6c8decded774b95a041d92/nodes/circuit.later_finite_size_comparison","semantic_class":"provenance_field_reference","source_field":"source_id","to":"sha256:f22708f3180068944c06829213f78f6ecfb65ef34f6c8decded774b95a041d92/sources/qaoa_finite_size_2026"},{"derived":true,"family":"provenance","from":"sha256:f22708f3180068944c06829213f78f6ecfb65ef34f6c8decded774b95a041d92/evidence/ordinary_comparison_warrants_20261024","id":"field:60b5f9995c97e3a43c7016aba27d0225368cc9033cb084131f74565b0e5b50ba","kind":"subject_ids","owner_ref":"sha256:f22708f3180068944c06829213f78f6ecfb65ef34f6c8decded774b95a041d92/evidence/ordinary_comparison_warrants_20261024","semantic_class":"provenance_field_reference","source_field":"subject_ids","to":"sha256:f22708f3180068944c06829213f78f6ecfb65ef34f6c8decded774b95a041d92/nodes/circuit.later_finite_size_comparison"},{"derived":true,"family":"provenance","from":"sha256:f22708f3180068944c06829213f78f6ecfb65ef34f6c8decded774b95a041d92/nodes/circuit.later_finite_size_comparison","id":"field:81e1ba1153f6231b65aacf7b82c5a6d21825b93cd33597a466930e234d4a042f","kind":"citation_ids","owner_ref":"sha256:f22708f3180068944c06829213f78f6ecfb65ef34f6c8decded774b95a041d92/nodes/circuit.later_finite_size_comparison","semantic_class":"provenance_field_reference","source_field":"citation_ids","to":"sha256:f22708f3180068944c06829213f78f6ecfb65ef34f6c8decded774b95a041d92/citations/qaoa_finite_size_corollary"},{"derived":true,"family":"provenance","from":"sha256:f22708f3180068944c06829213f78f6ecfb65ef34f6c8decded774b95a041d92/nodes/circuit.later_finite_size_comparison","id":"field:a9a889